<title>POLAND: COMPUTERLAND SEES 97 NET UP TO PLN 15 MLN.</title>
<headline>COMPUTERLAND SEES 97 NET UP TO PLN 15 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish software firm ComputerLand SA sees its net profit rising to 15.2 million zlotys in 1997 from last year's 11.2 million zlotys, the company said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>ComputerLand said its sales would likely grow to 255 million zlotys from 173.3 million zlotys in 1996.</p>
<p>The firm also said its subsidiaries would bring it an additional net profit of four million zlotys, after minority interest, on sales of 65 million zlotys.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
